
 # Set Operations

  Query and what it does :-

  Combine + dedupe ->
  SELECT id FROM a UNION SELECT id FROM b;

  Combine, keep duplicates (faster — no dedup pass) ->
  SELECT id FROM a UNION ALL SELECT id FROM b;

  Rows in both ->
  SELECT id FROM a INTERSECT SELECT id FROM b;

  Rows in a but not b ->
  SELECT id FROM a EXCEPT SELECT id FROM b; (MySQL: use NOT IN/LEFT JOIN pattern)
